nodecode-unbrowse is a rewrite of unbrowse-ai's unbrowse-ai/unbrowse:

  https://github.com/unbrowse-ai/unbrowse
  commit a82c59dfb05583836ecfa21fdc3f8a2ea73bfb76
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 Unbrowse AI (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the Hermes plugin's plugins/hermes folder — client.py (the hosted
MCP's JSON-RPC 2.0 client: the bearer key, the protocol-version header, a body
that is either JSON or the last event of an SSE stream, the server's own error
code carried through), tools.py (the 24 core tools of the shipped
tools.json, one handler between them, the dotted names, the isError rule and
the browser_capacity / unauthorized hints) and the operating guidance of
skills/unbrowse/SKILL.md, which became the manual topic the model reads. The
Python is not bundled: mcp.lisp speaks the same wire with nlk:http, and each
tool is a Lisp verb in the unbrowse package (unbrowse.scrape is
(unbrowse:scrape ...)), with unbrowse:call-tool reaching any tool the
workspace's tools/list carries and unbrowse:tools listing them.

Left out: the pre_tool_call browser guard and the web_extract backend, which
route Hermes' own built-in browser and extractor to Unbrowse — Nodecode ships
neither, so there is nothing to redirect and the manual tells the model to
read public pages with unbrowse:scrape. The Hermes settings file and env-var
layering became one section (the key is the section's api_key, with
UNBROWSE_API_KEY read when it is empty); the 24 model-facing tool
registrations became verbs taught by (help :unbrowse), Nodecode's vocabulary,
plus /unbrowse for the account's balance. The dynamic tools a workspace
learns stay reachable through unbrowse:call-tool rather than appearing as
tools of their own.
